n ten (10) days prior to the First Closing Date", "location": "EX-2.1, Section 10.2(e) — Conditions at the First Closing", "relevance_score": 5}, {"quote": "Each of the Company and the Acquisition Entities shall have delivered to Acquiror a certificate signed by an authorized director or officer of each of the Company and the Acquisition Entities certifying that the conditions specified in clauses (b), (c) (with respect to the Company and the Acquisition Entities), and (d) have been fulfilled;", "location": "EX-2.1, Section 10.2(f) — Conditions at the First Closing", "relevance_score": 5}, {"quote": "Acquiror shall have delivered to PubCo a certificate signed by an authorized director or officer of Acquiror certifying that the conditions specified in clauses (a), (c) (with respect to Acquiror), and (e) have been fulfilled.", "location": "EX-2.1, Section 10.2(g) — Conditions at the First Closing", "relevance_score": 5}, {"quote": "At the First Closing, the sum of (i) the amount of cash available in the Trust Account (after giving effect to all Acquiror Share Redemptions but prior to giving effect to the payment of any Acquiror Transaction Expenses or Company Transaction Expenses from the Trust Account) plus (ii) the aggregate gross proceeds that are actually received by, or unconditionally committed to be funded to PubCo pursuant to any Transaction Financing in connection with the transactions contemplated hereby, minus (iii) all Acquiror Transaction Expenses, minus (iv) all Company Transaction Expenses, shall be equal to or greater than $10,000,000 (the “Minimum Cash Condition”).", "location": "EX-2.1, Section 10.2(h) — Minimum Cash Condition", "relevance_score": 5}], "event_status": [{"quote": "On September 25, 2026, Harvard Ave Acquisition Corporation, a Cayman Islands exempted company (“HAVA” or “Acquiror”) entered into a business combination agreement", "location": "FORM 8-K, Item 1.01 — Business Combination Agreement", "relevance_score": 5}, {"quote": "The closing of the Proposed Transactions is subject to regulatory and shareholder approvals, and other customary closing conditions. No assurances can be made that the Proposed Transactions will be consummated on the terms or time frame currently contemplated, or at all.", "location": "EX-99.1 — Transaction Overview", "relevance_score": 5}], "security_description": [{"quote": "“Acquiror Class A Ordinary Shares” means Class A ordinary shares, par value $0.0001 per share, of Acquiror.", "location": "EX-2.1, Section 1.1 — Definitions", "relevance_score": 5}, {"quote": "each Acquiror Class A Ordinary Share (which, for the avoidance of doubt, includes the Acquiror Class A Ordinary Shares held as a result of the Unit Separation, Acquiror Right Conversion, and Acquiror Class B Ordinary Share Conversion) issued and outstanding immediately prior to the First Merger Effective Time (other than (1) any Acquiror Class A Ordinary Shares referred to in Section 3.1(a)(v), (2) Redeeming Acquiror Shares and (3) Dissenting Acquiror Shares) shall automatically be cancelled and cease to exist in exchange for the right to receive one newly issued PubCo Ordinary Share.", "location": "EX-2.1, Section 3.1(a)(iv) — Acquiror Class A Ordinary Shares", "relevance_score": 5}], "effective_date": [{"quote": "The First Merger shall become effective at the time when the Plan of First Merger is registered by the Cayman Registrar or at such later time permitted by the Cayman Companies Act as may be agreed by Merger Sub I and Acquiror in writing and specified in the Plan of First Merger, provided that such later time shall not be a date later than the second (2nd) Business Day after the date when the Plan of First Merger is filed and registered with the Cayman Registrar (the “First Merger Effective Time”).", "location": "EX-2.1, Section 2.2(a) — The First Merger", "relevance_score": 5}], "available_options": [{"quote": "“Acquiror Share Redemption” means the election of an eligible (as determined in accordance with Acquiror’s Governing Documents) holder of Acquiror Public Shares to redeem all or a portion of the Acquiror Public Shares held by such holder at the Acquiror Redemption Price.", "location": "EX-2.1, Section 1.1 — Definitions", "relevance_score": 5}, {"quote": "each Acquiror Class A Ordinary Share (which, for the avoidance of doubt, includes the Acquiror Class A Ordinary Shares held as a result of the Unit Separation, Acquiror Right Conversion, and Acquiror Class B Ordinary Share Conversion) issued and outstanding immediately prior to the First Merger Effective Time (other than (1) any Acquiror Class A Ordinary Shares referred to in Section 3.1(a)(v), (2) Redeeming Acquiror Shares and (3) Dissenting Acquiror Shares) shall automatically be cancelled and cease to exist in exchange for the right to receive one newly issued PubCo Ordinary Share.", "location": "EX-2.1, Section 3.1(a)(iv) — Acquiror Class A Ordinary Shares", "relevance_score": 5}, {"quote": "“Acquiror Redemption Price” means a per-share price, payable in cash, equal to the aggregate amount then on deposit in the Trust Account calculated as of two business days prior to the Second Closing, or such other time as agreed by Acquiror and the Company in writing including interest earned on the Trust Account (such interest shall be net of Taxes payable) and not previously released to the Acquiror to pay its Taxes, divided by the number of then issued Acquiror Public Shares, in connection with obtaining Acquiror Shareholder Approval.", "location": "EX-2.1, Section 1.1 — Definitions", "relevance_score": 5}], "default_option": [], "election_deadline": []}

